From: X570D4U OpenBMC adjustments <agross@therightstuff.de>
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: aspeed: x570d4u: Set VUART SIRQ4 active high

The host's ttyS0 stalls in interrupt mode with the default active-low
polarity. Active-high SIRQ4 restores host IRQ delivery and interactive
Serial over LAN on the X570D4U-2L2T.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/aspeed/aspeed-bmc-asrock-x570d4u.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/aspeed/aspeed-bmc-asrock-x570d4u.dts
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0+
 /dts-v1/;
 #include "aspeed-g5.dtsi"
 #include <dt-bindings/gpio/aspeed-gpio.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/interrupt-controller/irq.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/leds/common.h>
 
@@ -129,5 +130,6 @@
 
 &vuart {
+	aspeed,lpc-interrupts = <4 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
